# user_service — Cursor rules

Spring Boot 4.0.3 on Java 25. Source of truth for user identity in the EducationPlatform monorepo: registration, BCrypt credential check, profile data, role assignment, S3-backed profile photo.

## Package and layout

Package root: `org.example.user_service`. Port `8080`. Multipart cap 10MB.

```
domain/
  base/                         BaseEntity, BaseValueObject, BaseDomainEvent,
                                BaseDomainService, base/exceptions/
  user/
    User.java                   aggregate root
    events/                     CreateUserDomainEvent, ...
    ports/PasswordHasher        domain-owned port
    services/UserDomainService  state mutation + event recording
    vo/                         UserId, UserEmail, UserName, UserSurname,
                                UserPatronymic, UserStatus, UserPassword,
                                UserProfilePhotoLink, UserRole
application/
  exceptions/                   UserNotFoundException, UserAlreadyExistsException,
                                InvalidCredentialsException
  ports/                        UserRepo, PhotoStorage, EventBus, TransactionManager
  interactors/
    mappers/UserViewMapper
    user/<operation>/           one folder per use case: Command, Interactor, View
infrastructure/
  adapters/persistence/         HibernateUserRepo
  adapters/password_hasher/     PasswordHasherBcrypt
  adapters/s3/                  SeaweedFSUserProfilePhotoRepo
  adapters/event_bus/           SpringEventBus
  adapters/transactions/        SpringTransactionManagerAdapter
  event_handlers/               UserEventHandler
  persistence/models/           HibernateUser
  persistence/mappers/          UserMapperHibernate
presentation/http/v1/
  user/<operation>/{dto,handlers}/
  mappers/                      UserMapperCommand, UserMapperQuery
  exceptionHandlers/            ApiExceptionHandler, ErrorResponse
setup/config_beans/{user,s3,transaction,openapi}/
```

## Hard rules

- `PasswordHasher` is the only seam for hashing. BCrypt lives only in `infrastructure/adapters/password_hasher/`. Do not import `BCryptPasswordEncoder` from `application/`, `presentation/`, or any other adapter.
- `PhotoStorage` is the only seam for S3. `infrastructure/adapters/s3/SeaweedFSUserProfilePhotoRepo` is the only file in this service that may import `software.amazon.awssdk.*`.
- One folder per command under `application/interactors/user/<operation>/`. Do not collapse `change_name` / `change_surname` / `change_patronymic` / `change_status` into a single updater for new work.
- Mapping rules:
  - `UserMapperCommand` (presentation) — request DTO -> application command.
  - `UserMapperQuery` (presentation) — application view -> response DTO.
  - `UserMapperHibernate` (infrastructure) — domain `User` <-> `HibernateUser`.
  - All MapStruct. `lombok-mapstruct-binding` is wired in Gradle.
- Lombok is forbidden on `domain/` types. Allowed on Spring components, interactors, and JPA entities.
- Constructor injection only; no field `@Autowired`.
- DTOs are records under `presentation/http/v1/user/<op>/dto/`. Commands and views are records under `application/interactors/user/<op>/`. DTO types never cross into `application/`; commands never cross into `presentation/`.
- `MultipartFile` stops at the controller. Interactors receive `byte[]` + filename + content type via the command.
- Role assignment endpoints are admin-only. The gateway enforces this; the application layer re-checks.
- Domain events flow `UserDomainService` -> `EventBus.publish(...)` inside `TransactionManager.inTransaction(...)`. Never publish to RabbitMQ from a domain method — that is the outbox adapter's job.

## Tests

Every interactor under `application/interactors/user/<op>/` must have a matching `<Op>InteractorTest` at:

```
src/test/java/org/example/user_service/application/interactors/user/<op>/<Op>InteractorTest.java
```

Unit tests:

- AAA structure with explicit `// Arrange`, `// Act`, `// Assert` comments.
- Reuse `support/factories/UserFactory` and `support/factories/CreateUserCommandFactory` to build test data.
- Reuse `support/fakes/FakeUserRepo`, `FakePasswordHasher`, `CountingPasswordHasher`, `FakeEventBus`, `FakePhotoStorage`, `ImmediateTransactionManager`. Do NOT introduce Mockito unless a fake cannot express the case.
- AssertJ (`assertThat`) preferred over JUnit `assertEquals`.
- Behavior-first names. JUnit `@DisplayName` for the human-readable form.

Integration tests live in `src/integrationTest/java/...`, inherit from `support/integration/PostgresIntegrationTest` (Testcontainers PostgreSQL, `ddl-auto: create-drop`). Use them when behavior spans the JPA layer.

Domain VO and `UserDomainService` get their own unit-test files under `domain/user/{vo,services}/`.

## Linters and validation

Two tools wired into Gradle. Both run in CI and via pre-commit. **Never bypass them.**

- **Spotless** (`6.25.0`): unused imports, trailing whitespace, EOF newline, import order. Tasks: `spotlessCheck` / `spotlessApply`.
- **Checkstyle** (`10.18.2`): static checks (naming, braces, modifier order, missing override, no star imports, etc.). Config at `config/checkstyle/checkstyle.xml`. Tasks: `checkstyleMain`, `checkstyleTest`, `checkstyleIntegrationTest`.

If a single file is justifiably off-spec, use `@SuppressWarnings("checkstyle:RuleName")` plus a one-line reason. Do not edit `checkstyle.xml` to silence a single violation.

## Pre-commit

The repository ships `user_service/.pre-commit-config.yaml` using the [`pre-commit`](https://pre-commit.com/) framework. Install once:

```sh
pip install pre-commit
cd user_service
pre-commit install
pre-commit install --hook-type pre-push
```

Hooks: hygiene + Spotless + Checkstyle on commit, unit tests on push. Never `--no-verify`.

## Anti-patterns

- BCrypt imports inside `domain/` or `application/`.
- `software.amazon.awssdk.*` imports outside `infrastructure/adapters/s3/`.
- Role-check logic inside controllers (move to interactor; gateway is the outer fence).
- Mutable JPA-only domain objects, or returning `HibernateUser` from a port.
- Skipping `UserDomainService` and mutating `User` fields directly from an interactor.
- Adding a second password hashing algorithm or a second S3 adapter "for testing".

## Validation

From `user_service/`:

```sh
./gradlew spotlessApply       # auto-fix what can be fixed
./gradlew spotlessCheck       # verify clean
./gradlew checkstyleMain checkstyleTest checkstyleIntegrationTest
./gradlew test                # unit tests
./gradlew integrationTest     # Testcontainers (needs Docker)
./gradlew check               # all of the above + assemble
```

`./gradlew check` is the bar before commit. CI runs the same chain.
